/-
# The involutions in the reciprocity clause of `G1`

Node `G1` (`Work.SSGRoute.canonical_localPairing_with_reciprocity`) must supply its family of local
pairings together with the reciprocity clause (7): the sum of the local values of a pair of *global*
locally constant cocycles over one place per prime of `S'` and one involution per real place of `C'`
vanishes (this is the `hrec` hypothesis of `Work.SSGRoute.pt_selmer_relaxed`, pinned in this lane as
`H1Pair.PairReciprocity`).

This file records two facts about the archimedean part of that sum.

* `pairArchFamily_eq_zero_of_ne_two`: for `p ≠ 2` the archimedean family is *identically zero* at
  every involution group (`T`'s group is of order dividing `2`, whose order is invertible in `𝔽_p`,
  so all its `H¹` vanish; the explicit pairing `archPair` is `0` by definition for `p ≠ 2`).
  Consequently, for odd `p` the whole `C'`-part of the reciprocity sum vanishes, and the
  archimedean contribution to `G1` is confined to `p = 2` — the prime-2 correction of the paper.
* `pairReciprocity_of_vanishing_involutions`: correspondingly, reciprocity for a family whose values
  at the groups generated by involutions all vanish is *equivalent* to the finite-place reciprocity
  (the sum over `S'` of the local pairings at the decomposition groups), so a proof of the
  finite-place part suffices in that case.

Nothing here is a hypothesis about the finite places; the arithmetic content of reciprocity (the
global reciprocity law for the local invariants) is entirely in the `S'`-sum, and is *not* proved
here.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.Interfaces
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.DualMod.Main
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.E7Arch.pairFamily
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.H1Pair.Clauses
